-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 33, RULES 18 TO 28: PRELIMINARY ACTS; DEFAULT; SALE OF A SHIP; PAYMENT INTO COURT; DIRECTIONS; STAY.  LAYER 1.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
-- Written with a macro builder that quotes the source lines and writes the @ref; the builder is not part of this row, so edit this file directly.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  Every decision function answers `MAYBE BOOLEAN`.
--   JUST TRUE    the Rule says yes on these facts.
--   JUST FALSE   the Rule says no in its own words: a "means" definition, a flat negative, an "if" or "where" condition unmet,
--                a period fixed in the text's own words and missed.
--   NOTHING      the Rule does not answer: a duty not yet met, a power limited by its own wording, a list that is not closed, a silence.
-- A period is a Period constant plus a function over the last day of the period.  The last day is an INPUT, `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`:
-- the party states it as counted under Order 3, Rule 3.
-- SEAMS.  Inputs taken from outside this range: O 3 r 3 (the last day); O 6 r 6, 7 and 9 (default, defence, reply); O 9 r 7, 8, 9, 24 and 25;
-- O 13 r 2, 3 and 8; O 14 (summary judgment, applied by r 25(1)); O 15 r 1, 4 and 10; O 16 r 2; O 21 r 27 and 28; O 59 r 7.
-- "Deemed" in Order 33 has no definition of its own (O 28 r 1 defines it for Order 28 only).

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 33 -- Admiralty proceedings and marine insurance claims: rules 18 to 28`
-- ===========================================================================

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 18 -- preliminary acts`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- The preliminary act: a document in 2 parts.  One BOOLEAN per paragraph of Rule 18(2): whether the document states that matter.
DECLARE `o 33 r 18(2) preliminary act` HAS
    `o 33 r 18(2)(a) states the names of the ships and their ports of registry` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 33 r 18(2)(b) states the dimensions of the ship and its cargo` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 33 r 18(2)(c) states the date and time of the collision` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 33 r 18(2)(d) states the place of the collision` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 33 r 18(2)(e) states the wind` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 33 r 18(2)(f) states the weather` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 33 r 18(2)(g) states the tidal or other current` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 33 r 18(2)(h) states the position, course and speed when the other ship was first seen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 33 r 18(2)(i) states the lights or shapes carried` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 33 r 18(2)(j) states the radar echo of the other ship` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 33 r 18(2)(k) states the other ship when first seen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 33 r 18(2)(l) states the light or shape of the other ship first seen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 33 r 18(2)(m) states the other lights or shapes subsequently seen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 33 r 18(2)(n) states the alterations and measures taken to avoid the collision` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 33 r 18(2)(o) states the heading, the points of contact and the angle` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 33 r 18(2)(p) states the sound signals given` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 33 r 18(2)(q) states the sound signals heard` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 33 r 18(2)(r) states that the particulars in Part One are incorporated in Part Two` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 33 r 18(2)(s) states any other facts relied on` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 33 r 18(2)(t) states the allegations of negligence or other fault` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 33 r 18(2)(u) states the remedy or relief claimed` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:4773 | 18. —(1) In an action to enforce a claim for damage, loss of life or personal injury arising out of a collision between ships, the following provisions of this Rule apply unless the Court otherwise orders. (2) The claimant must within 2 months after service of the originating claim on any defendant, and the defendant must within 2 months after filing and serving a notice of intention to contest or not contest, file in the appropriate registry a document in 2 parts (called in these Rules a preliminary act) containing a statement of the following: Part One
-- src:4774 | ( a )
-- src:4775 | the names of the ships which came into collision and their ports of registry;
-- src:4776 | ( b )
-- src:4777 | the length, breadth, gross tonnage, horsepower and draught at the material time of the ship and the nature and tonnage of any cargo carried by the ship;
-- src:4778 | ( c )
-- src:4779 | the date and time (including the time zone) of the collision;
-- src:4780 | ( d )
-- src:4781 | the place of the collision;
-- src:4782 | ( e )
-- src:4783 | the direction and force of the wind;
-- src:4784 | ( f )
-- src:4785 | the state of the weather;
-- src:4786 | ( g )
-- src:4787 | the state, direction and force of the tidal or other current;
-- src:4788 | ( h )
-- src:4789 | the position, the course steered and speed through the water of the ship when the other ship was first seen or immediately before any measures were taken with reference to her presence, whichever was the earlier;
-- src:4790 | ( i )
-- src:4791 | the lights or shapes (if any) carried by the ship;
-- src:4792 | ( j )
-- src:4793 | the distance and bearing of the other ship if and when her echo was first observed by radar;
-- src:4794 | ( k )
-- src:4795 | the distance, bearing and approximate heading of the other ship when first seen;
-- src:4796 | ( l )
-- src:4797 | what light or shape or combination of lights or shapes (if any) of the other ship was first seen;
-- src:4798 | ( m )
-- src:4799 | what other lights or shapes or combinations of lights or shapes (if any) of the other ship were subsequently seen before the collision, and when;
-- src:4800 | ( n )
-- src:4801 | what alterations (if any) were made to the course and speed of the ship after the earlier of the 2 times referred to in sub ‑ paragraph ( h ) up to the time of the collision, and when, and what measures (if any) other than alterations of course or speed, were taken to avoid the collision, and when;
-- src:4802 | ( o )
-- src:4803 | the heading of the ship, the parts of each ship which first came into contact and the approximate angle between the 2 ships at the moment of contact;
-- src:4804 | ( p )
-- src:4805 | what sound signals (if any) were given, and when;
-- src:4806 | ( q )
-- src:4807 | what sound signals (if any) were heard from the other ship, and when;
@ref O 33 r 18(2) Part One (src:4773-4807)
GIVEN pa IS A `o 33 r 18(2) preliminary act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 33 r 18(2) Part One states every matter in paragraphs (a) to (q)` MEANS
    IF pa's `o 33 r 18(2)(a) states the names of the ships and their ports of registry` AND pa's `o 33 r 18(2)(b) states the dimensions of the ship and its cargo` AND pa's `o 33 r 18(2)(c) states the date and time of the collision` AND pa's `o 33 r 18(2)(d) states the place of the collision` AND pa's `o 33 r 18(2)(e) states the wind` AND pa's `o 33 r 18(2)(f) states the weather` AND pa's `o 33 r 18(2)(g) states the tidal or other current` AND pa's `o 33 r 18(2)(h) states the position, course and speed when the other ship was first seen` AND pa's `o 33 r 18(2)(i) states the lights or shapes carried` AND pa's `o 33 r 18(2)(j) states the radar echo of the other ship` AND pa's `o 33 r 18(2)(k) states the other ship when first seen` AND pa's `o 33 r 18(2)(l) states the light or shape of the other ship first seen` AND pa's `o 33 r 18(2)(m) states the other lights or shapes subsequently seen` AND pa's `o 33 r 18(2)(n) states the alterations and measures taken to avoid the collision` AND pa's `o 33 r 18(2)(o) states the heading, the points of contact and the angle` AND pa's `o 33 r 18(2)(p) states the sound signals given` AND pa's `o 33 r 18(2)(q) states the sound signals heard`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (a requirement not met; O 3 r 2(1) makes every requirement subject to the Court's discretion, so the text does not itself say no): "containing a statement of the following": a bare must, a matter not yet stated (open convention question QB)

-- src:4808 | Part Two
-- src:4809 | ( r )
-- src:4810 | a statement that the particulars in Part One are incorporated in Part Two;
-- src:4811 | ( s )
