-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 20 -- special provisions relating to collision, etc., actions`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- r 20(1): the claimant may not serve a reply or a defence to counterclaim except with the permission of the Court (open convention question QA).
-- src:4837 | 20. —(1) Despite anything in Order 6, Rule 9, the claimant in any action mentioned in Rule 3(1) may not serve a reply or a defence to counterclaim on the defendant except with the permission of the Court. (2) Every party to an action mentioned in Rule 3(1) must give production of any electronic track data that is or has been in the possession, custody or power of that party, by making and serving on every other party a list of all such electronic track data, and by making and filing an affidavit verifying that list and serving a copy of that affidavit on every other party — ( a )
@ref O 33 r 20(1) (src:4837)
GIVEN `the action is an action mentioned in Rule 3(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 33 r 20(1) the claimant may serve a reply or a defence to counterclaim on the defendant` MEANS
    IF `the action is an action mentioned in Rule 3(1)` AND `the person is the claimant`
    THEN IF `the Court has given permission`
         THEN JUST TRUE -- "except with the permission of the Court": with the permission the claimant may serve (open convention question QA)
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not serve a reply or a defence to counterclaim on the defendant except with the permission of the Court"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (1) speaks only of the claimant in an action mentioned in Rule 3(1)

-- src:4837 | 20. —(1) Despite anything in Order 6, Rule 9, the claimant in any action mentioned in Rule 3(1) may not serve a reply or a defence to counterclaim on the defendant except with the permission of the Court. (2) Every party to an action mentioned in Rule 3(1) must give production of any electronic track data that is or has been in the possession, custody or power of that party, by making and serving on every other party a list of all such electronic track data, and by making and filing an affidavit verifying that list and serving a copy of that affidavit on every other party — ( a )
-- src:4838 | in a case where the defendant disputes the jurisdiction of the Court by making an application under Order 9, Rule 7(2) — within 21 days after the disposal of that application; or
-- src:4839 | ( b )
-- src:4840 | in any other case — within 21 days after the defendant files and serves a notice of intention to contest or not contest.
@ref O 33 r 20(2) (src:4837-4840)
GIVEN `the action is an action mentioned in Rule 3(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party has electronic track data that is or has been in the possession, custody or power of that party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party makes and serves on every other party a list of all such electronic track data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party makes and files an affidavit verifying that list` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party serves a copy of that affidavit on every other party` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 33 r 20(2) the party gives production of electronic track data` MEANS
    IF `the action is an action mentioned in Rule 3(1)` AND `the party has electronic track data that is or has been in the possession, custody or power of that party`
    THEN IF `the party makes and serves on every other party a list of all such electronic track data` AND `the party makes and files an affidavit verifying that list` AND `the party serves a copy of that affidavit on every other party`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (a requirement not met; O 3 r 2(1) makes every requirement subject to the Court's discretion, so the text does not itself say no): "Every party to an action mentioned in Rule 3(1) must give production of any electronic track data that is or has been in the possession, custody or power of that party, by making and serving on every other party a list of all such electronic track data, and by making and filing an affidavit verifying that list and serving a copy of that affidavit on every other party" (a bare must not done; open convention question QB)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the trigger is unmet, so the duty does not arise; `o 33 r 20(2) the party gives production of electronic track data (the duty arises)` says so (open convention question QD)
@ref O 33 r 20(2) (src:4837-4840)
GIVEN `the action is an action mentioned in Rule 3(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party has electronic track data that is or has been in the possession, custody or power of that party` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 33 r 20(2) the party gives production of electronic track data (the duty arises)` MEANS
    IF `the action is an action mentioned in Rule 3(1)` AND `the party has electronic track data that is or has been in the possession, custody or power of that party`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every party to an action mentioned in Rule 3(1) must give production of any electronic track data that is or has been in the possession, custody or power of that party, by making and serving on every other party a list of all such electronic track data, and by making and filing an affidavit verifying that list and serving a copy of that affidavit on every other party"
