-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 21 -- judgment by default`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4843 | 21. —(1) Where an originating claim is served under Rule 7(8) on a party at whose instance a caveat against arrest was issued, then if — ( a )
-- src:4844 | the sum claimed in the action begun by originating claim does not exceed the amount specified in the undertaking given by that party or that party’s solicitor to procure the entry of the caveat; and
-- src:4845 | ( b )
-- src:4846 | that party or that party’s solicitor does not within 14 days after service of the originating claim fulfil the undertaking given by that party or that party’s solicitor as mentioned in sub‑paragraph ( a ),
-- src:4847 | the claimant may, after filing an affidavit verifying the facts on which the action is based, apply to the Court for judgment by default.
@ref O 33 r 21(1) (src:4843-4847)
GIVEN `the originating claim is served under Rule 7(8) on a party at whose instance a caveat against arrest was issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sum claimed in the action begun by originating claim does not exceed the amount specified in the undertaking given by that party or that party’s solicitor to procure the entry of the caveat` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that party or that party’s solicitor does not within 14 days after service of the originating claim fulfil the undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant, after filing an affidavit verifying the facts on which the action is based, applies to the Court for judgment by default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 33 r 21(1) the claimant may apply for judgment by default against the party who gave a caveat undertaking` MEANS
    IF `the originating claim is served under Rule 7(8) on a party at whose instance a caveat against arrest was issued` AND `the sum claimed in the action begun by originating claim does not exceed the amount specified in the undertaking given by that party or that party’s solicitor to procure the entry of the caveat` AND `that party or that party’s solicitor does not within 14 days after service of the originating claim fulfil the undertaking`
    THEN IF `the claimant, after filing an affidavit verifying the facts on which the action is based, applies to the Court for judgment by default`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where an originating claim is served under Rule 7(8) on a party at whose instance a caveat against arrest was issued, then if — the sum claimed in the action begun by originating claim does not exceed the amount specified in the undertaking given by that party or that party’s solicitor to procure the entry of the caveat; and that party or that party’s solicitor does not within 14 days after service of the originating claim fulfil the undertaking given by that party or that party’s solicitor as mentioned in sub‑paragraph (a), the claimant may, after filing an affidavit verifying the facts on which the action is based, apply to the Court for judgment by default"
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an originating claim is served under Rule 7(8) on a party at whose instance a caveat against arrest was issued, then if — the sum claimed in the action begun by originating claim does not exceed the amount specified in the undertaking given by that party or that party’s solicitor to procure the entry of the caveat; and that party or that party’s solicitor does not within 14 days after service of the originating claim fulfil the undertaking given by that party or that party’s solicitor as mentioned in sub‑paragraph (a), the claimant may, after filing an affidavit verifying the facts on which the action is based, apply to the Court for judgment by default"
-- src:4846 | that party or that party’s solicitor does not within 14 days after service of the originating claim fulfil the undertaking given by that party or that party’s solicitor as mentioned in sub‑paragraph ( a ),
