-- src:4848 | (2) Judgment given under paragraph (1) may be enforced by the arrest of the property against which the action was brought and by committal of the party at whose instance the caveat with respect to that property was entered.
@ref O 33 r 21(2) (src:4848)
GIVEN `judgment is given under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property against which the action was brought is arrested, or the party at whose instance the caveat with respect to that property was entered is committed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 33 r 21(2) judgment given under paragraph (1) may be enforced by arrest and committal` MEANS
    IF `judgment is given under paragraph (1)`
    THEN IF `the property against which the action was brought is arrested, or the party at whose instance the caveat with respect to that property was entered is committed`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "Judgment given under paragraph (1) may be enforced by the arrest of the property against which the action was brought and by committal of the party at whose instance the caveat with respect to that property was entered"
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Judgment given under paragraph (1) may be enforced by the arrest of the property against which the action was brought and by committal of the party at whose instance the caveat with respect to that property was entered"

-- r 21(3): in rem, no notice of intention to contest or not contest within the time: on the expiration of 14 days after service and upon filing the affidavits (and, if the statement of claim was not endorsed on the originating claim, a copy of it), the claimant may apply for judgment by default.
-- src:4849 | (3) Where a defendant to an action in rem fails to file and serve a notice of intention to contest or not contest within the time limited for filing such notice, then, on the expiration of 14 days after service of the originating claim and upon filing an affidavit proving due service of the originating claim, an affidavit verifying the facts on which the action is based and, if a statement of claim was not endorsed on the originating claim, a copy of the statement of claim, the claimant may apply to the Court for judgment by default.
@ref O 33 r 21(3) (src:4849)
GIVEN `a defendant to an action in rem fails to file and serve a notice of intention to contest or not contest within the time limited for filing such notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `14 days have expired after service of the originating claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant has filed an affidavit proving due service of the originating claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant has filed an affidavit verifying the facts on which the action is based` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a statement of claim was endorsed on the originating claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant has filed a copy of the statement of claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant applies to the Court for judgment by default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 33 r 21(3) the claimant may apply to the Court for judgment by default` MEANS
    IF `a defendant to an action in rem fails to file and serve a notice of intention to contest or not contest within the time limited for filing such notice` AND `14 days have expired after service of the originating claim` AND `the claimant has filed an affidavit proving due service of the originating claim` AND `the claimant has filed an affidavit verifying the facts on which the action is based` AND (`a statement of claim was endorsed on the originating claim` OR `the claimant has filed a copy of the statement of claim`)
    THEN IF `the claimant applies to the Court for judgment by default`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the claimant may apply": the power is not used
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "then, on the expiration of 14 days after service of the originating claim and upon filing an affidavit proving due service ... an affidavit verifying the facts ... and, if a statement of claim was not endorsed on the originating claim, a copy of the statement of claim"

