    IF `a defendant to a counterclaim in an action in rem fails to serve a defence to counterclaim on the defendant making the counterclaim` AND (NOT `the action is an action mentioned in Rule 3(1) and the defendant to the counterclaim is the claimant`) AND `the period fixed by these Rules for service of the defence to counterclaim has expired` AND `the defendant making the counterclaim has filed an affidavit stating that no defence to counterclaim was served during that period` AND `the defendant making the counterclaim has filed an affidavit verifying the facts on which the counterclaim is based` AND `the defendant making the counterclaim has filed a copy of the counterclaim`
    THEN IF `the defendant making the counterclaim applies to the Court for judgment by default`
         THEN JUST TRUE
