-- src:4924 | 28. Where an action in rem , being an action to enforce any claim mentioned in Rule 3(1), is begun and a cross action in rem arising out of the same collision or other occurrence as the firstmentioned action is subsequently begun, or a counterclaim arising out of that occurrence is made in the firstmentioned action, then — ( a )
-- src:4925 | if the ship in respect of or against which the firstmentioned action is brought has been arrested or security given to prevent her arrest; but
-- src:4926 | ( b )
-- src:4927 | the ship in respect of or against which the cross action is brought or the counterclaim made cannot be arrested and security has not been given to satisfy any judgment given in favour of the party bringing the cross action or making the counterclaim,
-- src:4928 | the Court may stay proceedings in the firstmentioned action until the security is given to satisfy any judgment given in favour of that party.
@ref O 33 r 28 (src:4924-4928)
GIVEN `an action in rem, being an action to enforce a claim mentioned in Rule 3(1), is begun` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a cross action in rem arising out of the same collision or other occurrence is subsequently begun, or a counterclaim arising out of that occurrence is made in the firstmentioned action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ship in respect of or against which the firstmentioned action is brought has been arrested or security has been given to prevent her arrest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ship in respect of or against which the cross action is brought or the counterclaim made cannot be arrested and security has not been given to satisfy any judgment given in favour of the party bringing the cross action or making the counterclaim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court stays proceedings in the firstmentioned action until the security is given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 33 r 28 the Court may stay proceedings in the firstmentioned action until security is given` MEANS
    IF `an action in rem, being an action to enforce a claim mentioned in Rule 3(1), is begun` AND `a cross action in rem arising out of the same collision or other occurrence is subsequently begun, or a counterclaim arising out of that occurrence is made in the firstmentioned action` AND `the ship in respect of or against which the firstmentioned action is brought has been arrested or security has been given to prevent her arrest` AND `the ship in respect of or against which the cross action is brought or the counterclaim made cannot be arrested and security has not been given to satisfy any judgment given in favour of the party bringing the cross action or making the counterclaim`
    THEN IF `the Court stays proceedings in the firstmentioned action until the security is given`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where an action in rem , being an action to enforce any claim mentioned in Rule 3(1), is begun and a cross action in rem arising out of the same collision or other occurrence as the firstmentioned action is subsequently begun, or a counterclaim arising out of that occurrence is made in the firstmentioned action, then — if the ship in respect of or against which the firstmentioned action is brought has been arrested or security given to prevent her arrest; but the ship in respect of or against which the cross action is brought or the counterclaim made cannot be arrested and security has not been given to satisfy any judgment given in favour of the party bringing the cross action or making the counterclaim, the Court may stay proceedings in the firstmentioned action until the security is given to satisfy any judgment given in favour of that party"
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an action in rem , being an action to enforce any claim mentioned in Rule 3(1), is begun and a cross action in rem arising out of the same collision or other occurrence as the firstmentioned action is subsequently begun, or a counterclaim arising out of that occurrence is made in the firstmentioned action, then — if the ship in respect of or against which the firstmentioned action is brought has been arrested or security given to prevent her arrest; but the ship in respect of or against which the cross action is brought or the counterclaim made cannot be arrested and security has not been given to satisfy any judgment given in favour of the party bringing the cross action or making the counterclaim, the Court may stay proceedings in the firstmentioned action until the security is given to satisfy any judgment given in favour of that party"
